      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Pinpoint, localized damage in a controlled environment, especially when the culprit vanishes overnight, suggests something very subtle, like a specialized, nocturnal pest or perhaps even a fungal/pathogenic agent with a microscopic entry point. You might need to consider mites, specific types of insect eggs that hatch at night, or even environmental factors like micro-abrasions from airflow patterns. It's a good idea to increase your sampling frequency, perhaps setting up sticky traps specifically during the night cycle to catch any nocturnal visitors.",
